  "verificationScope": "# SAME original CHAIN degree-one class and ACTUAL injective cocycle\n\nLET A be abelian with native Ext/derived structures,C the SAME ORIGINAL\nnonnegative chain complex,d_2:C_2->C_1 ZERO,C exact in EVERY positive\ndegree,N a coefficient object,I ANY actual injective resolution of N,\nand a:C_1->N ANY actual original top functional. Put E=coker(d_1),\nalpha=the SAME categorical quotient augmentation,and epsilon_C(a)=the\nSAME project originalChainTopExtClass C1alpha a. THEN CONSTRUCT\nb in Hom^0(C_0[0],I),c in Z^1 Hom(E[0],I),with\n d_1^* b = ofHom(single(a)>>I.iota),d(b)=pi^*c,\n epsilon_C(a) = Ext.delta_S^0(mk0(a)) = [c]_I,\n where S is the ACTUAL0->C_1->C_0->coker(d_1)->0 and\n [c]_I is EXACTLY native I.extEquivCohomologyClass.symm(mk c).\nThere is NO input lift,cone comparison,augmentation compatibility,\nExt-class equality,desired square,or global-projectivity assumption.\n\nCONSTRUCT gamma from SAME original chain via native extension n->-n\nand native mappingCone.lift. PROVE gamma retains SAME original quotient\naugmentation,then DERIVE gamma quasi-isomorphic from original positive\nexactness. PROVE native fst pulls back to SAME ordered identity top\ncocycle;native triangle third map is MINUS fst. Thus epsilon_C(id) is\nMINUS native short-exact roof. Native contravariant delta^0 contributes\nthe OTHER minus,so ANY original a gives EXACTLY the native boundary.\nReuse the immediately preceding PUBLIC constructed injective cocycle\nrealization. Generic source quasiiso/negative/congruence lemmas retain\nall actual augmentations and dependent quasiiso instances.\n\n13 declarations:11ordinary theorems and2CONSTRUCTED objects (NOT proofs).\n10individually compiled roots,393physical rootlines,22closed modules.\nAll13full imported types,2construction bodies,semantic roles and standard\naxiom closures manually read. Only propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound.\nALL12nonroot modules byte-match previous fully PUBLIC frozen archives.\n9native reference sources match pinned mathlib Git bytes after LF.\nThis is an ORIGINAL CHAIN degree-one computation under explicitly stated\nexactness/bound conditions,not yet the full original geometric theorem.\n\nOPEN:SAME arbitrary-r original ordered Koszul epsilon,source iterations,\nfull degree signs,actual a|S formula,geometric target/frame specialization,\nglobal-to-local isomorphism,proper-duality/canonical-theta,ambient twist\nand UNIFORM fixed m. Do not substitute this degree-one result for the\narbitrary-r manuscript. Keep original4.1/4.2/main OPEN,1<=r<n,d>=2,\nONE NONEMPTY parameteropen BEFORE ALLintegerk,and c distinct from finalQ.\nUnverified4.1 interface is NOTaxiom. GLOBAL Ext,INTERNAL SHEAF Ext and\naffine MODULE Ext stay distinct;local freeness is not global projectivity.\n\nKeep onecompiler,8GiBWindowsJob,2threads,CPU25%,BelowNormal,20min,\nallRAM/commit/disk thresholds,and ALLresourceholds. No agents,raised\nlimits or OSchanges. AlltaskfilesD. Wholelocalcheckpoint180;181notaccepted.\nNo whole-project replay or remote whole-project Lean CI claimed.\nLean4.35.0-rc3,pinnedmathlib2a885768dae569d938bb9ff3474da6a8753bb90a.\n",
